  "articleBody": "Exterior trim does far more than make windows and doors look attractive; it serves as a critical weather seal. When exterior boards start to crack, peel, or turn spongy, knowing when to call a general contractor prevents extensive interior repairs.\n\nLook for these clear warning signs:\n\n- Soft, spongy wood near window sills and door thresholds. If a screwdriver easily sinks into the trim, the wood has rotted and moisture has likely penetrated beneath it.\n- Detached boards with visible gaps behind siding or masonry. Exterior trim must integrate with flashing; detached boards allow wind-driven rain straight into wall framing.\n- Interior drywall staining adjacent to exterior trim. When water stains appear on interior sheetrock near window headers, exterior trim and flashing assemblies have failed.\n- Large-scale rot across multiple elevations. Widespread deterioration requires coordinated removal, substrate inspection, and professional replacement rather than small handyman patches.\n\nWhat to Expect During the Process\nA qualified contractor will inspect the surrounding flashings, remove damaged boards back to solid wood, allow adequate drying time, and install properly sealed, primed materials. As a BBB Accredited Business with an A+ rating, HH Remodeling LLC handles trim restoration and exterior repairs throughout Aurora, Littleton, and the Denver area. Call Abraham Becerra at 303-505-0866 to review your property.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
